          {
            "question": "How much can I compress my PDF files?",
            "answer": "Compression results vary significantly by content type. Image-heavy PDFs (presentations, scanned documents) typically achieve 40-70% size reduction. Text-heavy documents compress 15-30%. High-resolution scans can compress 70-85%. Documents already optimized may only compress 5-15%. Our tool automatically applies optimal settings based on your PDF content."
          },
          {
            "question": "Will PDF compression affect text quality or readability?",
            "answer": "No, text quality remains perfect. PDF compression doesn't affect vector text, fonts, or searchability. Only embedded images are optimized using smart quality settings that maintain visual clarity while reducing file size. All text remains crisp, selectable, and searchable exactly as in the original."
          },
          {
            "question": "Is my PDF data secure during compression?",
            "answer": "Absolutely! All compression happens locally in your browser using JavaScript and Web Workers. Your PDFs never leave your device or get uploaded to any server. We don't store, transmit, or access your documents. This ensures complete privacy and security for sensitive or confidential PDFs."
          },
          {
            "question": "What PDF features are preserved during compression?",
            "answer": "All essential features are preserved: text, formatting, fonts, hyperlinks, bookmarks, form fields, annotations, digital signatures, and document structure. Only embedded images are optimized and optional metadata is removed. Your compressed PDF maintains full functionality and compatibility."
          },
          {
            "question": "Can I compress password-protected or encrypted PDFs?",
            "answer": "Our tool currently works best with unprotected PDFs. If your PDF is password-protected, you'll need to remove the password first using Adobe Acrobat or other PDF tools, then compress it, and optionally re-apply password protection afterward. This ensures optimal compression results."
          },
          {
            "question": "How long does PDF compression take with your tool?",
            "answer": "Compression speed depends on file size and complexity. Typical PDFs (1-10MB) compress in 5-15 seconds. Large files (10-50MB) may take 30-60 seconds. Processing happens entirely on your device, so performance varies based on your computer's CPU power. All processing includes real-time progress updates."
          },
          {
            "question": "What's the difference between lossless and lossy PDF compression?",
            "answer": "Lossless compression (used for text and vectors) reduces size without any quality loss - perfect reconstruction is possible. Lossy compression (used for images) removes visually unimportant data for greater size reduction with minimal perceived quality loss. Our tool intelligently applies both methods: lossless for text/vectors, controlled lossy for images."
          },
          {
            "question": "Can I batch compress multiple PDF files at once?",
            "answer": "Currently our tool optimizes single PDF files for best results and fastest processing. For batch compression needs, you can process multiple files sequentially. We're planning to add batch processing in future updates based on user feedback and demand."
          },
          {
            "question": "Will compressed PDFs work on all devices and PDF readers?",
            "answer": "Yes! Compressed PDFs maintain full compatibility with all PDF readers and devices - Adobe Acrobat, web browsers, mobile apps, and operating system viewers. The compression process preserves PDF standard compliance, ensuring your documents work everywhere PDFs are supported."
          },
          {
            "question": "What's the maximum PDF file size I can compress?",
            "answer": "Our tool currently supports PDF files up to 50MB in size. This covers most common use cases - documents, presentations, reports, and moderate-resolution scanned files. For larger files, consider splitting them into smaller sections or using dedicated desktop PDF software for optimal results."
          },
          {
            "question": "Can I use the compressed PDF files commercially?",
            "answer": "Yes, absolutely! Compression doesn't affect your PDF's licensing or usage rights. The compressed file maintains all properties of the original - if you own the rights to the original PDF, you own the same rights to the compressed version. No watermarks, restrictions, or limitations are added during compression."
          }
